# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RestOS — KITCHEN / PASS SCREEN (apps/pass-kds). One file per PHYSICAL machine.
#
# Copy to kitchen.env on the kitchen machine, fill in from ops/ids.env, and load it from
# ops/startup/restos-kitchen.bat. Derived by grepping process.env and the *_ENV constants across
# apps/pass-kds/src and packages/device-config/src.
#
# ⚠ WITH THE COUNTER ROUTED `*=screen`, THIS SCREEN IS THE ONLY ROUTE FROM THE TILL TO A COOK.
#   If this machine is off, tickets are not queued anywhere else and nothing raises an alarm.
#   A station routed to a screen nobody is watching fails more quietly than a dead printer.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ identity ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Same org as the till and the API. From ops/ids.env: ORG_ID
RESTOS_ORG_ID=

# Same branch as the till — this screen shows THAT branch's queue. From ops/ids.env: BRANCH_ID
# WRONG VALUE: an empty queue, which looks exactly like a quiet kitchen.
RESTOS_BRANCH_ID=

# ⚠ ITS OWN id, DIFFERENT from the till's. From ops/ids.env: KITCHEN_DEVICE_ID
# Two apps sharing a device id share one store; two machines sharing one fork one outbox.
RESTOS_DEVICE_ID=


# ═══ cloud link ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ⚠ ORDERS REACH THIS SCREEN OVER THE WAN, not over the LAN. Nothing hosts the LAN mesh yet, so
#   a broken internet connection means the till keeps selling (00 §5.1) and this screen stops
#   receiving. That is a known gap, not a misconfiguration — plan the shift around it.
# Full WebSocket URL INCLUDING the path, same gateway as the till.
RESTOS_CLOUD_URL=ws://CLOUD_HOST:8080/sync

# Minted for THIS device id, with the kitchen class:
#   pnpm -C services/sync-gateway provision-device --org <ORG_ID> --branch <BRANCH_ID> \
#        --device <KITCHEN_DEVICE_ID> --class kitchen
RESTOS_DEVICE_TOKEN=


# ═══ staff ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Same dev seed as the till (see counter.env.example for the full warning). ONE KEY PER PERSON
# since August 2026 — one PIN for the whole roster was an authorization hole, because this screen
# seeds the SAME registry the till authorizes against, so a shared secret set here hands out the
# till's manager authority from the kitchen.
#
# COPY EACH PERSON'S DIGITS FROM counter.env EXACTLY. A person whose PIN differs between the two
# machines has two numbers to remember; a person left blank here is absent from THIS door only.
# All three blank = nobody can sign in, so nothing can be marked ready and no handover can be
# written — the queue fills and never empties.
#
# Signing in here grants no authority; it supplies attribution only (03-F53). The roles still
# matter for the till, not for this screen.
RESTOS_DEV_PIN=
RESTOS_DEV_PIN_BILAL=
RESTOS_DEV_PIN_HINA=


# ═══ who may say the food is ready ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# pass | kds | counter | waiter. Default `pass` — this screen draws a DONE control and a cook
# presses it. Set anything else and this screen becomes READ-ONLY for line states: the queue,
# the ages and the counts stay live, and the bump control is simply not drawn.
# ⚠ THIS IS A DIFFERENT LIST FROM RESTOS_SERVE_SIGNAL_OWNER. `kds` is valid here and invalid
#   there; `settlement` is valid there and meaningless here. Do not copy one into the other — an
#   unrecognised value falls back and reports itself on the boot line rather than refusing.
# RESTOS_READY_SIGNAL_OWNER=pass

# settlement | pass | counter | waiter — who owns the "food reached the customer" signal.
# ⚠ MUST BE THE SAME VALUE HERE AS ON THE TILL, or the two surfaces disagree about who owns
#   handover with every gate green. Default `settlement` on both; leave both unset.
# RESTOS_SERVE_SIGNAL_OWNER=settlement


# ═══ the rest — safe to leave unset ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Same one org policy as the till. If you set it there, set the identical string here: a counter
# reading neutral while the pass reads red is two surfaces disagreeing about whether food is late.
# RESTOS_AGING_THRESHOLDS=dine_in=10/20,delivery=15/25

# Pixels per inch of the actual glass. A kitchen screen is often a TV at a distance and is the
# most likely panel in the building to report nothing about its physical size — read the boot
# line, and if it says "assumed", measure the panel and set this. Range 50..800.
# RESTOS_PANEL_PPI=

# LAN mesh. Nothing hosts it yet; setting these changes a boot line and nothing else.
# RESTOS_LAN_PORT=7311
# RESTOS_LAN_HOST=0.0.0.0
# RESTOS_LAN_PEERS=<device_id>@192.168.1.10:7311

# Development only. Never set on a real screen.
# ELECTRON_RENDERER_URL=
